 }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\,\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=8$ independent exponential random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta ,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=\\theta {e}^{-\\theta x},\\,x\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}\\theta {e}^{-\\theta {x}_{i}} \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{n}\\,{e}^{-\\theta \\sum {x}_{i}} \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{n}\\,{e}^{-S\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}.$ \n\nWe are told that $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}=1$ and $n=8.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\theta }^{8}\\,{e}^{-\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192797 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6068f85b-0ea6-5161-a8d1-d4eb2504852b" :knowledge-point/title "Likelihood Functions for Exponential Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26dca0f2-85d0-5ea1-ac50-5d89df476c2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\theta }^{-5}\\,{e}^{15.8\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441692} {:answer/id #uuid "699a5a51-d732-56cb-a463-1fddf35d3809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\theta }^{15.8}\\,{e}^{-5\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441705} {:answer/id #uuid "dea83a2e-94b9-5271-9924-01ac2c1ec476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\theta }^{5}\\,{e}^{-15.8\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441748} {:answer/id #uuid "e94fa2bc-b583-577a-bd8e-a65df54b0519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\,{e}^{-5\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441754} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0e647a-a2d7-59e4-a4bd-0b321ff12df5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :ans